        "char_end": 689,
        "char_start": 573,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 257,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 258,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Therefore, $n$ can take any integer value from 0 to 10 inclusive, which gives us 11 possible values for $n$."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 787,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 788,
        "char_start": 690,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 294,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 295,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: For each value of $n$, there is a corresponding value of $x$ given by $x = (120 - n^2)^2$."
